{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066192-2e-werewolf-names","id":1066192,"title":"[2E] Werewolf Names","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-22T02:14:48-07:00","id":1066192,"title":"[2E] Werewolf Names","content":"I'm preparing some NPCs for coming 2E game - and have question related to the topic.<b> Are Uratha still use Deeds Names from 1E Werewolf corebook in modern times?</b> That means that they call themselves 'John Stormbringer' or 'Megan Goldenlocks'? Or are there other standards for naming characters? Maybe modern Uratha just use their pre-First Change names? But seeing how magic ( especially from mages ) works, more reason would be that they use some aliases than their birth names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:19:33-07:00","id":1066292,"title":"","content":"There are a few examples of deed names in the werewolf second edition book, so yes, but it does seem less prevalent or perhaps simply less emphasized. <br /> <br /> Also my impression always was that it was more like a replacement or AKA name and not an ammendment. More &quot;My friends call me John. You can call me Stormbringer.&quot; Than &quot;Hi, I'm John Stormbringer.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-22-2017, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:17:07-07:00","id":1066319,"title":"","content":"So who decides what the deed names are? Leaving the decision up to me is probably a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:23:27-07:00","id":1066365,"title":"","content":"In 1E it was assumed you got Deed Name by the Initiation Ceremony to your Tribe. Each Tribe put you against appropriate to it's nature challenge few days after First Change, and you got Deed Name by the Elder Uratha that run this thing, based on your actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-22-2017, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:13:37-07:00","id":1066422,"title":"","content":"OOC obviously the player does. But in character it is usually decided based on a deed the Uratha performed, I would assume usually bestowed by an elder (perhaps one overseeing an initiation trial) or their pack/peers. Hence deed name. They should be significant. They should have meaning, personal and symbolic. The Uratha has to have made an impression on someone, somewhere. An impression that they carry with them, that is tied to their reputation forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know, let\u2019s say a young Iron Master passes her initiation due to a series incredibly risky maneuvers that by all rights should have killed her. The elder overseeing the trial might deem her \u2018Nine Lives\u2019 to call attention to how lucky, or how bold she is. She wears it like a badge of honor, fortune favours the bold, she says. <br /> <br /> Or hell, perhaps the elder begrudges her her good luck. Perhaps he meant the trial to be overcome through cunning and skill and not good fortune. But a pass is a pass. In that case it might not even be a good name. She might be deemed \u2018Lucky Rabbit\u2019, and the name instead speaks of how she fled every danger and managed to escape unscathed. That name might haunt her as she tries to find a pack. Her peers might not take her seriously. But she might cleanse herself of the shame years later when she does something impressive enough, or just pays her dues long enough. Or hell, she might reclaim it. Nobody can catch her. She evades any trap, any ambush. The higher her Cunning grows, the more it becomes known that Lucky Rabbit is the slipperiest New Moon in town.<br /> <br /> <br /> Similarly a packmate who survives a hunter\u2019s silver bullet to the chest trying to protect his alpha, might still bear the wounds of that day. Perhaps even still feel fragments of silver lodged in his chest, aching anytime he shapeshifts. Regrouping later in their Den or whatever, one of his packmates (perhaps the Alpha) decides to call him Silverheart, and every time they call him by the name they are all remembering his his courage and his loyalty, and their luck at having made it through that encounter without losing anyone. The name means something deeply personal to them. To others, it tells them\u2026 \u201cHey, you know that one story you heard about the Blood Talon who survived 4 silver bullets to the chest and kept on trucking? That\u2019s him. That\u2019s the guy right there, and you just stepped onto his territory.\u201d<br /> <br /> That's my take anyway. Honestly there's not much guidance on this stuff, especially for 2e. That's how I use it. Not everyone has one, not everyone wants one, not everyone likes the one they got. But they mean something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-22-2017, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T23:17:39-07:00","id":1066713,"title":"","content":"I think of the kind of names Spirits would have, the deed name is the name of the wolf, the man is named John.<br /> This is the name Spirits would know him by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T23:45:43-07:00","id":1066721,"title":"","content":"But are they separate? So John is day-to-day, 'mortal' name? And Stormbringer is full and only name for Spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:01:04-07:00","id":1067300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066192-2e-werewolf-names?p=1066721#post1066721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are they separate? So John is day-to-day, 'mortal' name? And Stormbringer is full and only name for Spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, indubitably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:46:24-07:00","id":1067325,"title":"","content":"Spirits don't understand the concept of 'John', they do understand 'Flaming Claws of Death and Pain'.<br /> <br /> This also fits with the concept of Harmony; where does John end and Flaming Claws begin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:02:17-07:00","id":1067335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066192-2e-werewolf-names?p=1067325#post1067325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits don't understand the concept of 'John', they do understand 'Flaming Claws of Death and Pain'.<br /> <br /> This also fits with the concept of Harmony; where does John end and Flaming Claws begin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could also sorta deconstruct it when it comes to modern names. &quot;John&quot; comes from a word that means &quot;Graced by God,&quot; which <i>is</i> a concept a spirit would understand. We just tend not to know the origins of most of our names today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:04:04-07:00","id":1067404,"title":"","content":"In Dark Eras <i>Forsaken by Rome</i>, we have literal old Germanic Deeds Names like Hludawiga One-Eye, Herudis Deer-Sword and Rikirun the Sly - and similar where names in <i>Wolf and Raven </i>Era of Vikings. So I assume first, 'letters' part is for mortals only and spirits only take adjective part of name as truly meaning something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:40:52-07:00","id":1067518,"title":"","content":"I think there are probably different naming conventions. In the same way that there might be a stronger Modern American Uratha might have one word names like Ghost, Rend, Tango, Cash.<br /> <br /> <i>Adjectives the Noun </i>type stuff might be more old school (Runs the River Wild, Heeds the Whisper, Speaks like a Child, etc).<br /> <br /> So John the Baptist or Helga Longtooth might be more common in some eras or regions, who knows. But yeah, when I hear Helga Longtooth I do instinctively think it really means: Helga <i>aka</i> Longtooth, Or Helga 'Longtooth' Horvath. It's really up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T00:42:50-07:00","id":1067939,"title":"","content":"I've always mixed up how characters in my games treat deed-names, and the conventions they use. Some treat it as a suffix (e.g.: &quot;Irmgard the Stricken&quot;), while others use it more like a superhero's alter ego or an alternate name they use in different circles (Carl McPhee, aka &quot;Pays-the-Price&quot;). Others mix the two, with names like &quot;Max Headwound&quot; or &quot;Shotgun Annie&quot;. I like the idea of &quot;Verb-the-Noun&quot; names being more archaic, too.<br /> <br /> The most important thing for me, I think, is that the names MEAN something - they tell other Uratha (and spirits, although I think deed names are more important to the People, imo) something about them, whether it's a characteristic or an important deed from their past. <br /> <br /> In my current game, none of the PCs have a deed-name yet, but they're keeping an eye out for something to warrant it. I like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:43:53-07:00","id":1067977,"title":"","content":"I was going to offer more, but NateD summed up pretty much how I run Deed Names. You earn them through deeds or events, and they have a story of some sort behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T05:28:06-07:00","id":1074096,"title":"","content":"Looking over some inspirations for Deeds Names, I come to see Norse Kennings list, that works as nice examples list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_kennings\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_kennings\" target=\"_blank\"> List of kennings - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_kennings\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_kennings </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:41:06-07:00","id":1075666,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a hard fast rule, it seems to be something you're intended to utilize or ignore as you see fit. That said I imagine a name like Stormbringer would be easier to translate into First Tongue than John Taylor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}